      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic general text translation task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file translate_text.py using Microsoft/OpenAI.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] translate_text.py - translates a single text string between languages\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] batch_translate.py - translates a list of strings while preserving order\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] translate_markup.py - translates HTML or markup while preserving tags\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] translate_dictionary_values.py - translates dictionary values while preserving keys\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] translation_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for General Text Translation\n6. [HELPER] translation_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for General Text Translation\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] quality_summary.py - Summarize translation quality issues\n8. [LATER-STEP] unsafe_copy_check.py - Check localized copy for unsafe content\n9. [LATER-STEP] translation_memory_embedding.py - Embed translated segments for translation-memory search\n10. [LATER-STEP] localized_audio_preview.py - Generate spoken previews of translated copy\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
