      "data": {
        "text": "**Initiating Translation Project**\n\nI'm starting by establishing `translate_text.py` as the core, planning to integrate either Microsoft or OpenAI for the initial translation functionality. Once that's functional, the other nine Python files will be created, each leveraging a distinct external provider. It is important to remember to document each provider in the relevant code.\n\n\n**Developing Core Translation Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on `translate_text.py` using the OpenAI library, with a model selection pending. I'm also structuring `translation_client.py` and `translation_models.py` for helper functions. Furthermore, I'm identifying distinct providers for the remaining files, such as Google Cloud Translation, DeepL, AWS Translate, Cohere, and Azure Content Moderator, to ensure each utilizes a unique external service as required.\n\n\n**Refining Provider Assignments**\n\nI've firmed up the strategy, starting with `translate_text.py` using OpenAI and creating helper files `translation_client.py` and `translation_models.py`. I'm now assigning external providers to each file, ensuring uniqueness. Google Cloud Translation will handle `batch_translate.py`, AWS Translate is for `translate_markup.py`, and DeepL will be used for `translate_dictionary_values.py`. I'll employ Anthropic Claude for `quality_summary.py` and, after review, Azure Content Moderator for `unsafe_copy_check.py`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Module Structure**\n\nI've got the Phase 1 structure locked down, beginning with creating `translation_models.py` for the data models and then `translation_client.py`, which includes an OpenAI-specific translation client. After that, I will construct `translate_text.py` to instantiate and use that client. I'll define `TranslationRequest` and `TranslationResponse` dataclasses, alongside a `BaseTranslationClient` abstract class, for consistent interfaces. The OpenAI client will pull the API key securely from environment variables.\n\n\n**Defining Data Models & Client**\n\nI'm now focusing on Phase 1. I've decided to start with `translation_models.py`, defining `TranslationRequest` and `TranslationResponse` dataclasses. Following that, I'll create `translation_client.py`, which includes the `BaseTranslationClient` abstract class, and an `OpenAITranslationClient` implementation using the OpenAI API. The OpenAI client will pull the API key from an environment variable. Finally, I will write `translate_text.py` which instantiates and uses that client, using appropriate imports to identify the provider.\n\n\n",
